[Music]  hi  [Music]  so  the last time we caught up i was in the  southwest camping in a few new spots  exploring trails and getting out on  adventures utah in the spring is one of  my favorite places to be  the weather is perfect and there's so  many beautiful views  plus camping is easy and in most places  crowds are minimal  before utah i was pet sitting in durango  which is something i do  fairly often here and there to break up  long stretches of travel on the road  and to be honest i'm not sure i'd still  be out here if it weren't for those  breaks  [Music]  hey guys i'm christian schaefer i'm an  outdoor adventure photographer  and i've been living in my van full-time  for almost three years  so if you've been following for a little  while then you might remember a couple  months back i put out a video talking  about some of the struggles i've been  experiencing on the road  and just wanting to take a break well  right now i'm filming from jackson  wyoming and this is my new temporary  home  so around the one year mark of living on  the road i was living in my suv  and i just started to experience burnout  i would find myself scrolling airbnb for  week-long stays  month-long stays i even spent some time  apartment hunting in washington  and i was just kind of getting tired of  living on the road  i wanted some more stability so that's  when the idea of  pet sitting and house sitting came up  and it did take me a little while to get  that first  pet sit because i didn't have any  references and then after that it took  time to build experience and references  but it's been a two-year journey and  it's been so rewarding  and that's actually what i'm doing here  in jackson wyoming  i'm here for two whole months and i'll  be watching after an adorable wheaton  terrier named jack  and this is the longest set i've ever  done and i'm just really excited to be  here  also the owners are really rad jenna and  colin they're actually spending two  months at base camp in mount everest and  colin is attempting to climb mount  everest without supplemental oxygen  and then he'll be doing another high  peak immediately after that so  pretty badass we got this amazing van  taking us to the airport the airport  shuttle  ride ever i know that staying in a house  isn't  technically van life but house setting  has been  really helpful in keeping me out on the  road long term so  i just thought i would share this with  any of you who might be interested in  this lifestyle  so in general i have a sip booked every  two to three months  and they typically last one to two weeks  some of the longer ones have been three  weeks  and at first i found them through sites  that i signed up for  and now it's a mixture of that and also  just personal references and networking  i always tell myself during these days  especially the longer ones that i'm just  gonna like relax and unwind but that  almost  never happens usually my time is spent  tackling the many  to-do lists that are just kind of tricky  to do from the road  and there are a lot of van chores that  are so much easier to do from the house  for example  deep clean of all these dishes um  if you guys watch my van tour then you  know i don't actually have hot water  in my van so i do my best to clean it  when i'm on the road but whenever i get  a chance to run my stuff through a  dishwasher i  fully do that scheduled maintenance for  the van like oil changes  tire rotations factory recalls broken  windshields  washing the bedding and couch cushions  washing the floors  climbing up onto the roof to clean the  solar panels  pouring enzymes down the sink to keep it  from building up bacteria  cleaning dead bugs off the fan vent just  took this  thing off it's pretty gross gonna clean  that inside  and then just cleaning each of these  blades  they get pretty grimy clearing out and  wiping down the fridge  cleaning the toilet my personal favorite  so fresh  so clean applying fresh coats of finish  to the countertops  cocking the tile and trim and then there  are the usual chores like  washing the van filling the water tanks  filling the propane  and restocking supplies and that's just  the van stuff  so here's another great thing about  having a house to stay at  is when i have product shipments and  jobs i need to do  i have a lot of packing materials that i  have to get rid of and that'd be really  hard to do without a house  as a staging area besides all of that  there is washing the laundry  charging all of the electronics updating  software  uploading large files over wi-fi lining  up product shipments  ordering things online backing up hard  drives  um taking inventory of things in the van  i no longer need  sorry that's jack and and taking them to  a donation center  and forwarding my mail do you need to go  outside  [Music]  click  okay what was i talking about oh yeah  all the different things that  you have to do when you're staying at a  house um the most important thing of  course  is looking after the pets and it's my  favorite thing about  pet sitting is because i don't have a  dog on the road  and i just love animals so  house sitting and pet sitting gives me  an opportunity to spend some time with  them apart from the really long to do  list  the things i really look forward to are  just re-establishing  healthy routines and making space for  creativity and  contemplation relaxing  [Music]  [Music]  on the road so much of my time is just  devoted to planning routes around  photo shoots weather and product  shipments every day i have to think  about where am i going to sleep where am  i going to use the bathroom  where am i going to find wi-fi do i have  enough food propane and water  at least once a week i have to think  about where am i going to shower where  can i buy groceries and where can i  empty my trash  and empty my toilet and grey water tank  when i'm out on the road my mind is just  always in motion just keeping inventory  of these things taking steps to be safe  and in addition to these things i'm also  running a photography business from the  road  a lot of people call this lifestyle  living the dream including myself i love  living on the road  but it is not a walk in the park like  you have to put in the work  to keep this going for any length of  time if you're anything like me  that means you might need some breaks in  order to have balance so  this is my current reality living in a  beautiful corner of wyoming  with the world's cutest dog soaking up  some quality home time before hitting  the road again in june just in time for  summer  and getting out on some adventures in  the grand tetons and yellowstone  last fall i spent about three weeks  around jackson  and it was so beautiful i actually never  got around to sharing it so i'll show  you some of those clips here  i'm really excited to see how it looks  in spring this time around  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  so that's a little update and i actually  have a couple ideas for future videos um  but i'd love to hear in the comments  below which one you guys are most  interested in  i was thinking of putting together a  video about finances  um maybe how much i spend on a monthly  basis  while living in a van versus what i used  to spend in an apartment  maybe if any of you are interested in  this lifestyle you might get an idea of  how much you could save  and also just expenses to look out for  that you might not be aware of  another idea is a more in-depth video on  parking i touched on this topic briefly  but i was thinking i might do something  more in depth about  the experiences i've had the resources i  use  run-ins with cops things that will just  help you  find safe places out there on the road  because i know that was the number one  question i had before i moved into my  suv and also i would love to do an  updated van tour  so june of this year will be two full  years in the van  so i was thinking i might show you guys  an overview of what things i have  changed what things i  love what things i wish i had changed or  would do differently  um and just share some of the things  that have been working really well so  that's it thank you guys so much for  watching i hope you're all doing well  and quick housekeeping note if you want  to support me i've put  links down in my caption below to my  website and  there i have gear recommendations van  life essential recommendations  camping gear recommendations as well as  a lot of common questions like  what kind of van do i have how much did  it cost who built it  how i got started with photography all  of that stuff in one place i get a small  kickback every time you use those links  so  thank you so much i really appreciate  your support and i will see you next  time  or sooner if you find me over on  instagram  bye mr jack  you are so cute  you're so cute

